{"id": 33, "ts": 1780658256.994941, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah\u2019s provisional recommendation of Candidate\u202fA. While we still have no explicit observations of A\u2019s stress\u2011resilience or decision\u2011making under pressure, his proven ability to anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, and his very good leadership strongly suggest he can manage high\u2011stress, safety\u2011critical moments. Compared with the alternatives, Candidate\u202fC does demonstrate quick, correct decisions and excellent attention, but his egocentric attitude, difficulty communicating ideas, and lack of willingness to further his education raise serious concerns for crew cooperation and adaptability on long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fD shows strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility, yet his moodiness and loner reputation could impair cockpit teamwork. Candidate\u202fB, despite handling stress well, has clear red flags in crew cooperation and professional communication. Given that A\u2019s technical competence and leadership address the core safety requirements and the other candidates each have more pronounced deficits in cooperation, communication, or adaptability, I maintain my vote for Candidate\u202fA, while noting we should seek any additional evidence on his stress handling before finalizing."}
